Create a photorealistic cinematic film still, vertical frame. Plain solid BLACK background. In frame: only a heavy white piloted mech exosuit, a thin taut steel cable, and one broken concrete bridge slab with exposed rebar at the very top. The mech hangs motionless from the cable - at rest, NOT falling, no motion blur.

USE THREE REFERENCE IMAGES:
- POSE reference (the line sketch): copy this head-down diagonal hanging pose onto the mech, folded fairly tight at the hips, with these EXACT limb placements:
  - the HEAD / cockpit is the LOWEST point (lower-left), the TORSO runs diagonally up to the right;
  - the RIGHT ARM is raised and EXTENDED UP toward the legs - this is the FIRING arm the cable comes from;
  - the LEFT ARM hangs DOWN, loose, toward the head;
  - the RIGHT LEG is raised UP and to the UPPER-RIGHT, slightly bent at the knee;
  - the LEFT LEG is the TANGLED leg - the cable is wrapped around it.
- DESIGN reference (the robot): large white-and-grey armored exosuit, grey joints, exposed pistons and hydraulics, faded worn-yellow panels with red marks, scuffed battle-worn paint, open glass chest cockpit with a real human pilot (~170 cm) strapped inside.
- ARM-MECHANISM reference (the forearm close-up): the cable exits from the built-in CABLE LAUNCHER in the FOREARM near the WRIST - an open slotted housing with an internal pulley/spool threaded with the steel cable. The cable feeds out of THIS forearm launcher at the wrist, NOT from the palm or fingers.

THE CABLE (one continuous thin steel wire, in order):
1) it EXITS from the forearm cable-launcher at the WRIST of the RAISED RIGHT ARM and flies out in a STRAIGHT line;
2) that straight line meets the LEFT LEG and the cable WRAPS AND TANGLES around the left leg's SHIN (tibia area) - looping around the lower leg so it is caught and snarled;
3) from the tangled left shin the cable continues onward and UP, pulled perfectly TAUT and STRAIGHT, to a grapple hook snagged in the broken bridge slab at the top - one straight tight line, not curved, not slack.
The cable is thin - a pencil-thin braided steel wire, dark grey, NOT a thick rope.

Lighting: natural soft directional light against the black void, realistic highlights on the worn white metal, desaturated cinematic. ARRI Alexa LF, sharp still frame, no motion blur, fine film grain, grime, scratches, chipped paint. Photorealistic, highly detailed, true-to-life, no cartoon, no CGI look.

